# Chapterize JS: core rules

**North star: be the best and most modern way to automatically add a table of contents to a preexisting page DOM.**
Zero-dependency TOC + scrollspy by Byron Johnson; "the accessible, attribute-only Tocbot alternative".
Name: **Chapterize JS** (npm `chapterize-js`, global `Chapterize`); never hard-code it, use `scripts/brand.mjs` / `{{name}}`. v0.1.0, published to npm on 2026-10-28.
Full context: `docs/PROJECT-GOALS.md`; quick start: `AGENTS.md`. This repo is the library only (GitHub + npm);
the website is the sibling repo `chapterize-js-site`, in production at https://chapterizejs.com (it vendors this repo's `dist/`, README, llms.txt; see AGENTS.md).

## Goals (never regress one to help another)
1. Simpler than Tocbot: attributes only, zero JS config, auto ids.
2. Zero deps; core `dist/index.min.js` < 5 KB gzip soft limit (now 5,037 B, 2026-10-28). Report the number when `src/` changes.
3. Most beautiful: opt-in gliding marker (`line`, `pill`, `minimal`).
4. Accessibility first: `aria-current`, auto label, focus to section, reduced motion = instant.
5. Correct: last/short sections, offsets, first click, CSS smooth scroll, hash routers.
6. Every framework + plain sites: SSR-safe, auto-init, DOM watching, idempotent, destroy/refresh.

## Invariants
- Modern features always have a fallback; never depend on one missing in Chromium, Firefox or WebKit.
- CSSOM only for styles (CSP-safe); no `<style>`/`style=""` strings. The site (sibling repo) runs under CSP `script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'`.
- `data-chapter*`, `.is-active`, `.is-trail`, `chapter:change`, `--chapter-*`, `@layer chapter` are frozen unless Byron says otherwise.

## Approvals (hard stop)
- Never `npm publish`, `git push`, `git init`, deploy, log in to services, or touch other folders (e.g. `/workspace/scrollspy-demo` (the original prototype), `/workspace/ghost-reveal`) without Byron's explicit OK.
- Ask before breaking changes (renamed attributes/events, changed defaults).

## Working habits
- Byron edits files himself: re-read a file right before editing and keep his changes.
- Don't invent facts (sizes, support, download counts, "tested with X"). Measure, cite, date; say what wasn't run.
- Before reporting: `npm run test:all` green in all three engines (and the site's `npm run test:all` if the change shows on the site).
- Design taste: dark, editorial, distinctive; no icon-above-title cards; effects add no load weight.
- User-facing copy: follow `.cursor/skills/write-docs/SKILL.md`. State what the library does before any jargon.
